# Tech Stack Decisions — Unit: pr-review-agent

| Concern | Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Agent language | **Python 3.11** | Matches existing `app/`; enables Hypothesis for PBT; already installed on the runner via `setup-python`. |
| Review engine | **Kiro CLI (headless)** — `kiro-cli chat --no-interactive` | User decision (2026-09-17). Agentic, repo-aware reviewer. |
| Engine auth | **`KIRO_API_KEY`** (GitHub Actions secret) | Documented Kiro CLI headless/CI auth method. No AWS IAM/Bedrock needed. |
| Kiro CLI install | **Pinned-version install step** in the workflow (download official binary) | Q2=A. Reproducible builds; satisfies SECURITY-10 (no floating `latest`). Version pinned via `KIRO_CLI_VERSION` env. |
| GitHub API client | **`gh` CLI** (`gh api`, `gh pr review`, status via `gh api`) authenticated with `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` | Q1=C. Minimal Python deps; `gh` is well-maintained and commonly present; auth via built-in token. |
| Subprocess handling | Python `subprocess.run` with explicit `timeout`, arg lists (no shell string interpolation) | Prevents command injection (SECURITY-05); enforces timeout (fail-closed). |
| PBT framework | **Hypothesis** | PBT-09; Python-native, strong shrinking + seed reproducibility. |
| Example-based tests | **pytest** | Matches existing `app/tests`. |
| Output contract | Kiro CLI instructed to emit **strict JSON** (findings array with severity/category/file/line/title/detail) | Enables deterministic, pure `compute_verdict` + PBT round-trip properties. |
| Dependency pinning | `requirements.txt` with exact versions; `gh` and `kiro-cli` pinned | SECURITY-10. |

## Configuration (environment variables)
| Var | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `KIRO_API_KEY` | (secret) | Kiro CLI auth |
| `GH_TOKEN` | `GITHUB_TOKEN` | gh CLI auth (least-privilege scopes) |
| `KIRO_CLI_VERSION` | pinned | Kiro CLI version to install |
| `MAX_DIFF_BYTES` | `204800` (~200 KB) | Oversized-PR skip threshold (Q3=B) |
| `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `300` (5 min) | Per-invocation timeout, fail-closed (Q4=A) |
| `BASE_BRANCH` | `dev` | Branch the agent reviews PRs against |

## Rejected Alternatives
- **PyGithub / requests**: rejected in favor of `gh` CLI (Q1=C) to minimize Python deps and reuse the runner's token-based auth.
- **Pre-baked CLI in runner image**: rejected (Q2) — pinned install step is more reproducible and auditable.
